 ## Bundled browser VNC viewer
 
 noVNC 1.7.0 by the noVNC authors, primarily Mozilla Public License 2.0; its incorporated pako files use the MIT license and other notices are retained in the upstream source. Unmodified pinned JavaScript source, complete upstream LICENSE.txt/AUTHORS, component notices, release URL and archive SHA-256 are in `vendor/noVNC/`. The owned HTTP viewer serves the source modules and `/novnc/LICENSE.txt` and `/novnc/UPSTREAM.json` offline. noVNC upstream: https://github.com/novnc/noVNC/releases/tag/v1.7.0 . Local integration in `assets/vnc-browser/` and `src/services/vnc/browser.rs` is TermCraft code.
+
+Local original-package inspection uses zip 9.8.2 (MIT) and lzma-rs 0.3.0 (MIT), with CRC/crc-catalog (MIT OR Apache-2.0), typed-path (MIT OR Apache-2.0), constant_time_eq (CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0 OR Apache-2.0), and zeroize_derive (MIT OR Apache-2.0) as pinned in Cargo.lock. These independently implemented codecs decode user-selected archive bytes; original packages, executables, DLLs and other vendor assets are not bundled. Dependency source and licenses are recorded under `docs/parity-evidence/legacy-package-import/`.
